      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Is there any update on this bug? Using ulong with bit shifting is super efficient for sending more networked data without bogging it down or reaching the networking limits.\nMost worlds are going to have to send twice as much network data because of this bug forcing us to use less efficient data types.\nI wrote a significant amount of code I spent all day on, only to find out this data type no longer works.\nTested on the latest SDK version as of Jan 12 2021: VRCSDK3-WORLD-2020.12.09.04.44_Public",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
